prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: a production PIXEL ART animation sprite sheet for a mobile focus timer, real transparent PNG.
Create exactly EIGHT frames of ONE cute gray tabby cat's UPPER BODY in a strict 4-COLUMN × 2-ROW grid, read left-to-right on top row then left-to-right on bottom row. Square 1024×1024 canvas; all eight cells are identical 256×512 rectangles. No visible grid lines, no labels, no numbers, no text.
Pixel style: genuinely crisp hand-crafted retro game pixel art. Each cell is designed on a 64×128 logical pixel grid, enlarged exactly 4× with nearest-neighbor square pixels. Flat limited palette of 6 neutral gray shades plus one dark charcoal outline. Big clean pixel clusters, stepped silhouettes, readable little tabby stripes, subtle dither-free pixel highlights. No photographic fur, no brush texture, no smooth gradients, no 3D rendering, NO antialiasing, NO blur. Warm and adorable despite the gray palette. Designed for charcoal #272727 UI.
Character and viewpoint: look DOWN onto the cat from above and behind. Cat faces DOWNWARD toward the bottom of each frame. Only its upper back, the BACK of its head, two small ears seen from behind, shoulders, and two FRONT legs are visible. Never draw a face: NO EYES, NO NOSE, NO MOUTH, no front-facing portrait. NO TAIL, NO RUMP, NO HIND LEGS, NO BELLY. The upper back is a short cropped torso with a flat cropped upper edge; no full animal body.
Frame registration: exactly the SAME body/head position, scale, stripe pattern, palette, camera, and horizontal center in every cell. Upper edge of the cropped torso at local y=32 pixels, centered around local x=128 pixels; ample transparent side margins. Head and left foreleg stay almost fixed. The viewer's RIGHT front leg performs the gesture. Keep every part inside its own cell with at least 16 transparent pixels between it and the cell boundaries except the deliberately cropped upper back. Do not shift the whole sprite between cells; screen entry/exit will be animated separately in code.
Eight distinct poses:
1. relaxed upper body, right forepaw retracted near the head;
2. right foreleg begins reaching down;
3. right foreleg extends noticeably farther downward;
4. right forepaw reaches the lowest stamping contact point;
5. right forepaw presses flat, slightly wider and compressed by two logical pixels, head makes a tiny downward nod;
6. right forepaw lifts a little, returning to rounded shape;
7. right foreleg withdraws halfway;
8. right forepaw returns to the original relaxed pose matching frame 1.
The left forepaw remains higher than the stamping right paw in the contact poses.
Absolutely NO separate paw-print mark inside the frames; the app draws the ink print separately. No scenery, floor, cast shadow, props, borders or UI. Genuine transparent alpha background. This must be an animation-ready consistent eight-frame sprite sheet, NOT eight different cats or a decorative collage.
